  "deviations_from_floorplan": [
    "Extra M3 VSS shield on y 66.9 um between the COMP_P and CMP_CLK stubs into the SAR pins, tied to the corridor shields at x 88.4-90.8. Without it the routes added 60 aF more CLK coupling to COMP_P than to COMP_N (trial adc-core-route-c2-pex); with it 10.5 aF (adc-core-route-c3-pex).",
    "The 73.5 um channel shield starts at x 48.215 (east edge of top_fill_exclusion_inputs) instead of 47.3: with a 0.1 um width its lower edge entered that TOP fill exclusion by 0.035 um.",
    "The VSS shields form one floating net (VSS_SHIELD, 15.5 fF, no device terminals); the VSS tie belongs to the supply stage. Parasitics count shield coupling as load.",
    "Wires are 0.1 um wide; layer changes use two cuts per level (0.13 um pitch). The CMP_CLK drop is 0.05 um wide over the core and lands with one VIA3 on the existing M3_M2 via (decisions.cmp_clk_north_drop)."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Typical-corner flat xRC only; no CWORST/CBEST extraction of the routed core.",
    "Delays are Elmore bounds between device terminals with coupling grounded (no Miller factor) and 1 fF per receiver gate; no transient was run (no ADC simulation in this stage).",
    "Resistances and delays include the blocks' own pin-side wiring and gate resistance, so they bound the route-only values from above.",
    "No fill, no fill-exclusion layers drawn; density DRC stays deferred to top-level fill.",
    "Out of scope and not drawn: D0-D7, SAMPLE, VINN/VINP, ADC.* boundary pins, VREF and supply feeds, the SAR guard ring and the decoupling."
  ],
